WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.490
- Hey, Legal Eagles.

00:00:01.490 --> 00:00:04.600
There are a lot of
extracurriculars available

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:06.190
to students in law school.

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:08.760
But the choices can seem overwhelming.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:12.440
They are very different from
what you can do in college.

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:14.920
So what extracurriculars are out there

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:17.890
and what should you spend
your time on in law school?

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:19.050
Well by the end of this video

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:20.740
you will have a really good idea

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:23.240
of which extracurricular is for you.

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:24.920
What will add to your resume

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:28.130
and what is a good use of
your time in law school.

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:29.128
So stick around.

00:00:29.128 --> 00:00:33.045
(melodious instrumental music)

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:36.090
All right, so first and foremost.

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:39.490
Extracurriculars can be
very rewarding in law school

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:40.800
but generally speaking,

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.770
grades are more important
when you're in law school.

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:45.610
So while it may be tempting to sign up

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:47.350
for lots of extracurriculars

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:49.790
especially during the first week of class.

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:50.780
As a general rule,

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:53.570
you never want to sacrifice your grades

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:56.950
for spending time in
extracurricular activities.

00:00:56.950 --> 00:01:00.020
And that goes for even the most
prestigious extracurriculars

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:02.410
like participating on law review.

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:05.290
It's almost always better
to have good grades

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:08.630
than it is to participate
in lots of extracurriculars.

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:11.180
So with that being said
and without further ado,

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:14.520
here are the most popular
extracurriculars in law school

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:17.390
and my opinion as to
how valuable they are.

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:19.510
And I should tell you I
know what I'm talking about.

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:22.560
In addition to working in
BigLaw for over 10 years,

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:24.990
I have recruited for big firms,

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:28.620
I have interviewed many law
students for associate jobs

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:30.960
and I have read more law student resumes

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:32.580
than I could possibly count.

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:35.240
So, let's talk about the most popular

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:37.190
extracurriculars in law school.

00:01:37.190 --> 00:01:39.400
The first one and the most popular

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:43.210
and usually the most highly
regarded is law review.

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:46.980
Generally, law schools have
one flagship law review.

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:51.090
A law review is a weird
student-run publication

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:54.130
that publishes papers by
professors, professionals

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:55.573
and other academics.

00:01:56.470 --> 00:01:59.360
While other fields have
peer reviewed journals

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:03.160
that are run by professionals
or experts in the field.

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:07.110
Law schools have these
student-run publications

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:08.200
that do two things.

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:12.440
They review, curate and
proof the academic papers

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:15.820
mostly of professors
and then publish them.

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:18.380
And Law Reviews will publish the papers

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:21.020
of students who are on law review

00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:22.200
and those are called notes.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:23.930
Sometimes without attribution

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:27.010
to the individual student who produced it.

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:29.120
but the law review serves the purpose

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:30.990
of publishing academic papers.

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:33.880
They tend to be the most
prestigious legal journals

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:34.970
in the legal field

00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:38.020
and they also publish
the papers of students.

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:40.420
Now if you want to publish in law school

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:42.210
you should join law review.

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:45.590
There are, generally, also
a lot of other journals

00:02:45.590 --> 00:02:48.880
or law reviews that specialize
in different topics.

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:52.350
But almost always the
most prestigious journal

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:56.320
in a particularly is law
school the law review.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:58.070
And there are a couple very famous ones,

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:00.560
the Harvard Law Review comes to mind.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:05.460
It's an incubator for future
professors and legal scholars.

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:06.730
It's really the top of the field

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:09.060
when it comes to legal publications.

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:11.290
And while there are a number

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:14.020
of different journals and
law reviews in law school,

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:17.840
generally, the main law review
is the most prestigious,

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:20.290
it can be a real resume bump.

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:23.420
Out of all the things that
you can do in law school

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:24.380
as an extracurricular,

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:28.630
there is no doubt that participating
in the Maine Law Review

00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:31.120
for your law school is by far

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:33.660
the most prestigious
extracurricular that you can do.

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:35.160
It is a real resume bump

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:37.560
especially when you get
to the top law schools

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:39.150
where the law review itself

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:42.600
has an actual reputation in the field.

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:45.080
But that being said, it
is a ton of hard work.

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:49.020
You are constantly proofing
and reviewing different papers,

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:51.380
only a few of which are
going to be published.

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:53.570
It's really thankless work.

00:03:53.570 --> 00:03:55.310
It is very persnickety,

00:03:55.310 --> 00:03:58.170
you have to have a real eye for proofing,

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:00.430
you have to be a very good writer

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:04.160
and it's also very difficult
to get on to the law review.

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:07.600
Some law reviews require
you to have top grades

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:08.860
before you can participate

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:11.720
and other law reviews have a
straight merit-based system

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:14.400
based on writing on to the journal.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:17.870
So you show a writing sample
and that's how you get on.

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:20.380
Other law reviews have
a combination of the two

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:21.877
where some people will grade on

00:04:21.877 --> 00:04:24.310
and some people will write on.

00:04:24.310 --> 00:04:26.010
But once you get on to law review

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:29.000
you can anticipate that you're
going to spend a lot of time

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:32.230
doing writing related
activities, a lot of proofing

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:34.423
and a lot of publishing related work.

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:38.320
So that brings me to
the second most popular

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:41.363
extracurricular in law school
and that is moot court.

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:44.050
Moot court is where students

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:46.600
pretend to be appellate attorneys.

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:48.910
Students will write appellate briefs

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:50.980
and then they will argue that brief

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:53.360
usually on a very narrow part of the law

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:55.230
in front of a panel of judges.

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:57.990
This panel of judges is
sometimes real judges

00:04:57.990 --> 00:05:01.530
if the school is able to get
the judges to participate.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:04.670
But usually some lawyers
from the community

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:07.330
who are judging the
students on their ability

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:10.380
to argue on either the appellate brief

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:15.380
and/or their oral argument
ability in front of them.

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:17.820
There are a number of
different moot courts,

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:21.910
some specialize in
international law or patent law.

00:05:21.910 --> 00:05:24.540
And some are just sort of a general civil

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:26.950
or criminal appellate jurisdiction

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:31.260
where they'll give you a
topic that is of wide appeal

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:34.060
and you'll argue that particular topic.

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:37.370
Some moot courts are just
for the particular school

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:40.240
where it's just amongst
students in that school.

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:45.140
And some are against schools
from around the city or state

00:05:45.140 --> 00:05:48.060
where students will be
competing against each other.

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:50.010
In some moot courts
you're graded on the brief

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:51.990
and some it's just your oral argument

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:54.613
and some is a combination of the two.

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:59.100
Now moot court is certainly a resume bump,

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:00.920
not as much as law review.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:02.550
But if you have moot court,

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:06.700
especially if you are a
successful moot court competitor

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:11.470
then employers will look
favorably on that in your resume.

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:14.010
Especially if you can
show that you are someone

00:06:14.010 --> 00:06:16.930
who was very good at arguing,
very good at writing,

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:17.790
those are the kind of skills

00:06:17.790 --> 00:06:19.610
that future employers want to see.

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:21.860
So it's not quite as
prestigious as law review

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:24.930
and it's not quite as much
of a bump in your resume

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:27.110
but it's certainly a positive mark

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:28.900
on your law school resume.

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:32.230
It's also a great way to hone
your oral argument skills.

00:06:32.230 --> 00:06:34.630
It feels like, there's a
bit of a bait-and-switch

00:06:34.630 --> 00:06:35.570
when you get to law school

00:06:35.570 --> 00:06:38.110
where you think you're gonna
be arguing all the time

00:06:38.110 --> 00:06:40.260
but really you're just
sitting in a lecture hall

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:41.610
listening to your professor.

00:06:41.610 --> 00:06:44.190
And at most you're going back and forth

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:45.190
in the Socratic method

00:06:45.190 --> 00:06:48.100
when he or she peppers you with questions.

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:49.610
But this is one of the true places

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:53.010
where you are able to
get better at arguing

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:58.010
and have a chance to compete
in that type of competition.

00:06:58.130 --> 00:07:00.700
So that brings me to the third most common

00:07:00.700 --> 00:07:04.870
extracurricular in law school
and that is mock trial.

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:07.330
Don't get mock trial
and moot court confused.

00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:11.550
If moot court is a simulation
of appellate advocacy

00:07:11.550 --> 00:07:16.320
then mock trial is a
simulation of a real trial

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:18.370
at the trial court level.

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:21.350
I did both moot court and
mock trial in law school

00:07:21.350 --> 00:07:24.730
and while moot court is a
lot of fun and it's great,

00:07:24.730 --> 00:07:27.460
I thought mock trial was way more fun.

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:29.930
You get to do all the aspects of a trial.

00:07:29.930 --> 00:07:31.260
You guys to do opening statement,

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:34.320
examination of witnesses,
cross examinations,

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:36.450
closings, objections.

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:41.260
It's like Law &amp; Order but
in real life but still fake,

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:43.000
if that makes sense.

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:45.290
It's not dissimilar to mock trial

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:47.150
in high school or in college

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:49.873
but it's operating at a much higher level.

00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:53.880
There are different mock
trials and they vary by topic.

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:55.240
There are civil mock trials,

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:57.670
there are criminal mock
trial competitions,

00:07:57.670 --> 00:08:00.730
there are employment
mock trial competitions,

00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:02.240
there are a lot of different formats too.

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:05.720
In some mock trials you
provide your own witnesses,

00:08:05.720 --> 00:08:07.770
in other words their fellow law students

00:08:07.770 --> 00:08:10.160
who are training to be a witness

00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:11.760
and you prep them ahead of time.

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:14.010
And in some mock trials,

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:18.500
the competition actually
gives you a witness

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:19.560
that you've never met before

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:21.450
and you only have a couple
of minutes to prep them

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:24.580
before they go on the witness stand.

00:08:24.580 --> 00:08:26.380
So there are a lot of different venues

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:28.780
that can be a lot of fun to participate in

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:30.560
because they're so varied.

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:33.680
Mock trial is probably less prestigious

00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:36.110
than law review and moot court.

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:39.260
But I would say that people
in the know really understand

00:08:39.260 --> 00:08:41.520
that mock trial is an incubator

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:44.080
for people who really want to be in court.

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:47.160
So you can show that you have the skills

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:49.490
of a real practicing trial attorney

00:08:49.490 --> 00:08:52.040
if you hone them in mock trial.

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:54.500
So while it's not quite
as much of a resume boost

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:56.700
as moot court and law review,

00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:58.390
it's still something
that's worthwhile doing

00:08:58.390 --> 00:09:00.620
if you're prepared for
the time commitment.

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:04.460
So that brings me to the next
extracurricular in law school.

00:09:04.460 --> 00:09:06.330
It is by far the most popular

00:09:06.330 --> 00:09:07.163
and it's the one that

00:09:07.163 --> 00:09:09.430
almost every law student participates in

00:09:09.430 --> 00:09:12.040
and that is drinking.

00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:14.490
There's a lot of drinking in law school.

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:17.420
I'm talking in jest, that
is an extracurricular.

00:09:17.420 --> 00:09:19.260
But I am telling you this for two reasons.

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:21.410
One is that, your social life

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:23.640
is an important aspect of law school.

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:26.040
You should go out and you
should meet other people

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:28.210
and have a little fun on occasion.

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:30.350
And number two is that,

00:09:30.350 --> 00:09:32.950
when people go out to go drinking

00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:34.960
they usually call it bar review.

00:09:34.960 --> 00:09:36.840
And the first time anyone ever hears

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:39.530
that they're going to bar
review on Thursday night,

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:42.010
they often make the assumption
that it's a study group,

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:42.843
it's not.

00:09:42.843 --> 00:09:45.083
Bar review means going out for drinks.

00:09:45.990 --> 00:09:49.780
Just FYI, you have been
warned, it happens.

00:09:49.780 --> 00:09:53.240
And you know, go out once
in a while, it's worthwhile.

00:09:53.240 --> 00:09:56.380
Okay, so back to all seriousness,

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:57.800
the next extracurricular

00:09:57.800 --> 00:10:01.810
is the various student groups on campus.

00:10:01.810 --> 00:10:04.420
There are a lot of student
groups in law school,

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:06.560
you have human rights groups,

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:09.380
you have ethnic and cultural groups,

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:13.360
the Federalist Society,
outlaw, Black Law Students.

00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:18.200
There are a lot of social
groups and cultural groups that,

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:19.670
it's sort of a loose association,

00:10:19.670 --> 00:10:22.803
they try and bring speakers in,
they often hold conferences.

00:10:23.780 --> 00:10:26.430
This isn't that much of a resume boost

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:28.100
but it's a great way to network,

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:30.250
so I wouldn't discount it entirely.

00:10:30.250 --> 00:10:32.480
It's also a good way to meet friends

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:34.350
and other attorneys in the community

00:10:34.350 --> 00:10:37.380
who share similar values to you.

00:10:37.380 --> 00:10:39.450
So you know a part of law school

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:42.050
that most people overlook is networking.

00:10:42.050 --> 00:10:44.090
And you should spend some time

00:10:44.090 --> 00:10:46.310
getting to know people in the community

00:10:46.310 --> 00:10:48.890
especially if you want to
work in that community.

00:10:48.890 --> 00:10:50.740
Because it's a great way to form

00:10:50.740 --> 00:10:52.700
a social network of your own

00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:55.770
that may come in handy when
you're looking for jobs

00:10:55.770 --> 00:10:57.060
later down the line.

00:10:57.060 --> 00:11:00.210
So after that, I would say
the last big extracurricular

00:11:00.210 --> 00:11:02.950
are social committees in law school.

00:11:02.950 --> 00:11:06.350
These are things like
participating on law prom,

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:09.070
putting together the big
dance for law students.

00:11:09.070 --> 00:11:11.220
If your school has a law school musical,

00:11:11.220 --> 00:11:13.000
putting together the musical.

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:15.010
There are also public interest committees

00:11:15.010 --> 00:11:18.380
and various fundraising activities.

00:11:18.380 --> 00:11:20.670
Again like the social organizations

00:11:20.670 --> 00:11:23.630
these are not necessarily
a big resume boosters

00:11:23.630 --> 00:11:25.260
but they're great for networking

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:28.220
and a great way to spend
some time on something

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:32.510
other than the black letter
law in your particular classes

00:11:32.510 --> 00:11:34.570
which you know sometimes
we get tunnel vision

00:11:34.570 --> 00:11:37.500
and we focus just on studying

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:39.930
and not other social
aspects of law school.

00:11:39.930 --> 00:11:43.190
So don't discount the
social committees as well.

00:11:43.190 --> 00:11:44.690
Now if you want even more information

